    "pricing-options",
    "Pricing Options",
    "1948022",
    "<p>ZBrush for iPad is now included with all ZBrush and Maxon One subscriptions, and it’s also available as a stand-alone subscription. And for anyone who wants to try the world’s leading digital sculpting application, there's also a free version. Both versions are available on the App Store, and the robust free version includes an introductory set of 28 of the most popular brushes and limited features for tools like Dynamesh, SculptrisPro, ZSpheres, and ZRemesher.</p>",
